  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-stakeholder workshop on biodigesters in Senegal (CERF24SN3I)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity supported the organisation and facilitation of a multi-stakeholder workshop on biodigesters in Senegal, held in November 2024.The workshop&#x2022;	gathered government agencies, private sector actors, knowledge institutions, and non-governmental organisations (NGOs) to develop a strategic roadmap for scaling bio-waste-to-energy solutions.&#x2022;	built on findings from a Climate and Energy Response Facility (CERF)-funded study that analysed organic waste potential, market players, and sector challenges.&#x2022;	discussions addressed governance, financial models, and technology deployment.&#x2022;	outcomes included recommendations for policy alignment, private sector engagement, and financing mechanisms.&#x2022;	strengthened Dutch-Senegalese cooperation in bio-energy and supported future interventions in aid, trade, and diplomacy.</narrative>
  </description>
